        intuition: `Real-world data is rarely a straight line; chemical reactions, car braking distances, and rocket trajectories curve. Polynomial regression fits these curves by expanding features [x, x², x³]. But high-degree polynomials wiggle wildly to memorize noise! Regularization adds a mathematical tax (penalty) on weight magnitude, forcing the curve to stay smooth and generalizable.`,
