        workedExample: `Step-by-Step Z-Score Normalization Trace:\nTraining feature values: [10, 20, 30]. Unseen test value: [40]:\n1. Mean μ_train = (10 + 20 + 30) / 3 = 60 / 3 = 20.0\n2. Variance σ²_train = [ (10-20)² + (20-20)² + (30-20)² ] / 3 = [100 + 0 + 100] / 3 = 200 / 3 = 66.67\n3. Std Dev σ_train = √66.67 = 8.165\n4. Scaled Training Set:\n   z₁ = (10 − 20) / 8.165 = −1.225\n   z₂ = (20 − 20) / 8.165 = 0.000\n   z₃ = (30 − 20) / 8.165 = +1.225\n5. Scaled Test Sample (NEVER recompute mean! Use μ_train and σ_train):\n   z_test = (40 − 20.0) / 8.165 = +2.449. Leak-free transformation complete!`,
        codeSnippet: `from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer
from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder
from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer
from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier

# Complete Leak-Free Multi-Type Pipeline:
num_pipe = Pipeline([
    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median')),
    ('scaler', StandardScaler())
])

cat_pipe = Pipeline([
    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')),
    ('onehot', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False))
])

preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(transformers=[
    ('num', num_pipe, ['age', 'income', 'credit_score']),
    ('cat', cat_pipe, ['education', 'marital_status'])
])

full_model = Pipeline([
    ('prep', preprocessor),
    ('clf', RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42))
])
# full_model.fit(X_train, y_train)
# y_pred = full_model.predict(X_test)`
