        workedExample: `Step-by-Step Population Stability Index (PSI) Drift Trace:\nCredit Score bin [600, 650]: Expected (Training) = 20% (0.20), Actual (Live) = 35% (0.35):\n1. Difference: Actual − Expected = 0.35 − 0.20 = +0.15\n2. Ratio: Actual / Expected = 0.35 / 0.20 = 1.75\n3. Logarithm: ln(1.75) = 0.5596\n4. Bin PSI Contribution: 0.15 × 0.5596 = 0.0839\n5. Across all bins, total PSI = 0.28 (> 0.25 threshold!) ⟹ ALERT: Severe Data Drift detected; automated retraining pipeline triggered!`,
