            desc: `THE 3 ESTIMATORS EXPLAINED:
• LGBMClassifier: Scikit-Learn wrapper for classification (churn, fraud, image labels). Target y must be discrete integers {0, 1} or {0..K-1}. Objective is 'binary' (Binary Log-Loss) or 'multiclass' (Softmax Cross-Entropy). Provides .predict() for hard labels and .predict_proba() for calibrated probabilities.
• LGBMRegressor: Scikit-Learn wrapper for continuous numeric targets (house price, stock return, temperature). Objective is 'regression' (Average Squared Error L2), 'regression_l1' (Average Error Size L1), 'huber' (outlier-robust), or 'quantile' (predicting 10th or 90th percentile bounds). Provides .predict() returning real floats.
• LGBMRanker: Specialized learning-to-rank engine for search engines (Google/Bing) and eCommerce item recommendations. Objective is 'lambdarank' (optimizes LambdaMART gradient of NDCG). CRITICAL REQUIREMENT: Requires the 'group' argument in .fit(X, y, group=query_lengths) specifying how many search results belong to each query (e.g. group=[10, 15, 8]). Items are ranked strictly within their query session, never across sessions!`,
